Subject: [PATCH 07229/11362] [outer-loop] bp35 L9 mapping round 19: corrects
 round 18 (door shaft goes UP, no pillar eye)

Seventh round on bp35 L9, still honest null. Correction + new tool:
- NEW TOOL: f.frame is a multi-layer FIXED-camera animation array exposing the
  player's absolute vertical trajectory (up/down), hidden by the camera-relative
  settled frame. Built bp35_l9_traj.py.
- RETRACTS round 18's pillar-eye claim: the door-shaft LEFT death is the player
  RISING row37->row0 (passing row20 unharmed) and flying off the open shaft top.
  Shaft goes UP, away from the goal (below). Verified 3x.
- Flip-up before shaft entry survives but only returns to the up-gravity pocket.
- No move/click from the fall-through landing descends toward the goal.
- REFINES round 18: color-12 toggle blocks absent (0 cells) in every live state;
  only in the GAME_OVER overview, not live-usable.

Goal stays topologically sealed. Frontier stays at level 8. Next lead: test whether
L9's win is an activate/collect condition, not diamond-touch navigation.

